From: Zortos <zortosdev@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:27:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] shader: interpolate noperspective varyings
 perspective-correct (OoT tomb red line, port of #722) (#820)

* shader: interpolate noperspective varyings perspective-correct (#441)

Ocarina of Time draws water volumes whose vertex shader writes a
screen-space coordinate (clip.xy / clip.w) as a noperspective varying.
When a vertex sits next to or behind the camera (w close to 0), the
primitive is clipped and the attribute has to be re-interpolated at the
clip points. On AMD (RDNA3, Windows driver) that produces wrong values:
the fragment shader samples its depth input far off, computes a negative
distance and exp2 overflows to the R11G11B10 maximum. This is the red
dotted line in the Royal Family's Tomb.

Emulate noperspective with perspective interpolation instead: the last
pre-rasterization stage (vertex, tessellation evaluation or geometry)
writes the value times Position.w, and the fragment stage reads it
perspective-correct and multiplies by FragCoord.w (1/w). The result is
the same screen-linear value, and clipping now interpolates it correctly.

Mesh pipelines are left unchanged: the fragment stage only converts its
inputs when the previous stage scaled them. EDEN_NX2_NOPERSP_AS_SMOOTH=0
turns the emulation off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* shader: keep noperspective emulation out of XFB, indexed loads and repeated EmitVertex

Review follow-ups for the perspective-correct noperspective emulation:

- Skip the emulation when transform feedback is enabled or the fragment
  program reads attributes indexed. Transform feedback would capture the
  value times Position.w, and the indexed load path does not multiply by
  FragCoord.w. Producer and fragment stage decide together, so those
  pipelines keep native noperspective interpolation.
- Geometry shaders keep output values across EmitVertex. An output that
  is written once and emitted several times was scaled by every vertex's
  w in turn. Restore the unscaled values after each EmitVertex, like the
  fixed pipeline point size.
- Assert instead of silently skipping the FragCoord.w multiply; only
  float inputs are marked and DefineInputs forces FragCoord for them.
- Wrap three lines to the 100-column limit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* shader: always interpolate noperspective varyings perspective-correct

Drop the EDEN_NX2_NOPERSP_AS_SMOOTH switch from #722 so the fix ships
unconditionally.

* shader: keep native noperspective varyings with passthrough geometry

A passthrough geometry shader can write generics outside its passthrough
mask, and those aren't scaled by Position.w, so the fragment stage must not
divide them.

